# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# Always revalidate code + content so a push shows up immediately instead of
# being served from a stale cache. (Images keep default caching — they get new
# filenames when they change, so they're safe to cache.)
#
# ⚠️ THIS LIST IS LOAD-BEARING, AND A TYPE THAT IS MISSING FROM IT IS PUBLISHED
# FOR SEVEN DAYS AFTER YOU DELETE IT (VR-167, 9/6).
#
# Anything not matched here falls to Pages' default `public, s-maxage=604800`.
# That is a 7-day EDGE cache, not a browser one, so it is not something the
# reader can refresh past and not something a deploy clears: a cached response
# is served without the origin being consulted at all.
#
# Found the hard way. VR-164 took `.claude/agents/release-steward.md` out of git
# on 9/5 — correctly, and the origin was clean immediately: the per-deployment
# URL 404'd. The production hostname kept serving the file anyway, because `.md`
# was not on this list. Measured 9/6: `cf-cache-status: HIT`, `age: 73693`.
#
# THE RULE THAT FOLLOWS: removing a file from the repo is not unpublishing it.
# `_leakcheck.js` proves nothing withheld is in `git ls-files`; nothing proves
# the edge has caught up. For a `*.pages.dev` hostname there is no self-serve
# purge — Purge Cache is zone-scoped and that zone is Cloudflare's, not ours —
# so the only lever is making sure the thing was never cacheable in the first
# place. That is what this file is for.
#
# So: ADD A TYPE HERE BEFORE YOU COMMIT ONE. Text served from this repo is
# world-readable (CLAUDE.md §5) and should also be world-*revocable*.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Markdown is served, not just stored — CLAUDE.md and every harness's sibling
# notes are live at guessable URLs. Added VR-167.
/*.md
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Nothing links to these and they are all published anyway: the harnesses'
# Python tooling, the confidential-terms-adjacent text formats, and any JSON
# that is not a build artifact. Cheap to revalidate, expensive to leave stuck.
/*.py
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.txt
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
